docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md:16:- The Files sidebar section changes nothing but one thing: it creates a new empty file or a new empty folder, because the developer asked for it ([issue #349](https://github.com/heidrun-org/heidrun/issues/349)). It has no button to rename, move, delete, or edit a file.
docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md:17:- The header stays at the top of the sidebar section while the rows scroll under it. It holds the title "Files" and five buttons that show only an icon, in this order: "New file", "New folder", "Refresh", "Collapse all folders" (the icon `dash-square`), and "More options" (three vertical dots).
docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md:19:- The folder tree uses the same list of files as the Files window: the files that Git tracks, the new files, and the folders that `.gitignore` ignores only when the option to show ignored files is on, as folders that do not unfold. Folders come first, then files, in alphabetical order. Each row shows, from the left: one indent guide for each level of depth, a slot for the arrow of a folder, the icon of a folder or of the kind of the file, the name, and for a changed file a colored status letter at the right. A file keeps the slot of the arrow empty, so the names of the files and of the folders of one level line up. The icons are grey, not colored.
docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md:25:- A right click on the row of a file opens a context menu at the pointer ([issue #383](https://github.com/heidrun-org/heidrun/issues/383)). A context menu is a small menu that opens at the pointer. It has two items, in this order: "Copy absolute path" puts the absolute path of the file on the clipboard, and "Copy relative path" puts the path of the file on the clipboard, relative to the folder of the workspace. After a copy, a toast shows the text that was copied. The key Escape, a click outside the context menu, or a click on an item closes the context menu. The context menu stays inside the window. The row of a folder has no context menu. A copy changes no file, so the Files sidebar section still only reads files.
docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md:28:- The icon `folder2` of the Files sidebar section is the first icon of the sidebar icon bar of the left sidebar, above the Scripts icon. It shows no number.
docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/index.md:17:- [files.md](files.md): the Files sidebar section.
docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/chats/chats_header_and_sort.md:14:  1. "Sort by": "Created on" (the date of the first record that has a date, or the date of the file when no record has a date), "Last updated" (the date of the file of the chat), "Messages from you" (the number of messages that the developer typed), "Issues" (the number of issues that the chat mentions), "Pull requests" (the number of pull requests that the chat mentions), and "Files written" (the number of different files that the coding agent wrote, a file of a worktree and the same file at the root counting as one).
docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/README.md:12:Read `sidebars.md` for the sidebars and the notes. Read `source_control.md` for the Source control section. Read `code_hosting.md` for the Code hosting section, and `code_hosting_search.md` for its search field and its saved searches. Read `files.md` for the Files section. Read the folder `chats` for the Chats section.
docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/sidebars.md:15:- The left sidebar holds the Files sidebar section, the Scripts sidebar section, the Source control sidebar section, and the Code hosting sidebar section, in this order from the top.
docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/sidebars.md:18:- The sidebar icon bar shows one icon for each sidebar section, one under the other: `folder2` for the Files sidebar section, `play-circle` for the Scripts sidebar section, `git` for the Source control sidebar section, `github` or `gitlab` for the Code hosting sidebar section (a `cloud` when the hosting service is not known, see [code_hosting.md](code_hosting.md)), `bell` for the Needs you sidebar section, `sticky` for the Notes sidebar section, and `chat-left-text` for the Chats sidebar section. The title of the sidebar section is the tooltip of its icon. The number of a sidebar section sits on the top right corner of its icon.
